Subject: [PATCH 7/7] docs/bpf: explain the CPUMAP RFS sample and its
 boundaries

Describe socket CPU observations, stable tuple domains and ordered hash
fallbacks. Document how to build, configure, attach and drain the sample,
including its static topology and ingress quiescence requirements.

State the supported packet and socket paths, early-lookup limitations,
process failure behavior, and the outstanding performance evaluation.
Distinguish selection counters from successful packet delivery and show
how to run the policy and infrastructure selftests.

